# Workflow: Skill Auto-Integration

Purpose:
  Automatically integrate recommended skills into the project.
  Triggered when skill gap analysis finds missing skills with >= 80% relevance.
  Creates actionable plan and executes integration with human approval.

## Auto-Integration Triggers

Automatic Triggers:
  - Skill gap analysis finds >= 80% relevant skill
  - New technology added to project
  - New feature requiring new skill
  - External best practice discovered

Manual Triggers:
  - Human requests skill addition
  - Human approves recommendation
  - Periodic skill audit

## Auto-Integration Workflow

  1. SKILL DISCOVERY
     - Analyze project requirements
     - Scan .sdd/skills/ registry
     - Check external sources (old/external-repo-audit/)
     - Identify candidate skills

  2. RELEVANCE SCORING
     - Calculate relevance for each candidate
     - Domain match: 40%
     - Technology match: 30%
     - Use case match: 20%
     - Maturity: 10%
     - Filter: score >= 80%

  3. GAP ANALYSIS
     - Compare against current skills
     - Identify overlaps
     - Identify duplicates
     - Calculate coverage improvement

  4. RECOMMENDATION
     - Generate recommendation report
     - Priority order
     - Integration plan
     - Estimated effort
     - Present to human

  5. HUMAN APPROVAL
     - Human reviews recommendation
     - Human approves/rejects/modifies
     - Human sets priority
     - Human provides context

  6. SKILL ACQUISITION
     - Copy from .sdd/skills/ if exists
     - Adapt from external source if needed
     - Create new skill if necessary
     - Follow SKILL-EXECUTION format

  7. SKILL ADAPTATION
     - Adapt to project context
     - Update examples
     - Update validation criteria
     - Update dependencies
     - Test skill execution

  8. SKILL INTEGRATION
     - Add to .sdd/skills/<domain>/INDEX.sdd
     - Add to .sdd/INDEX.sdd navigation
     - Update .sdd/skills/INDEX.sdd ReadOrder
     - Create DEC-XXX for addition
     - Update README.md

  9. SKILL TESTING
     - Test skill execution
     - Validate input/output
     - Check examples
     - Verify fallback behavior

  10. SKILL DEPLOYMENT
      - Deploy to .sdd/skills/
      - Update registries
      - Notify agents
      - Document in README

  11. KNOWLEDGE SHARING
      - Share new skill with all agents
      - Update skill cache
      - Notify dependent skills
      - Document lessons learned

## Auto-Integration Rules

  [AI1] Only skills with >= 80% relevance are auto-recommended.
  [AI2] Human approval is required before integration.
  [AI3] Duplicate skills are not integrated.
  [AI4] Experimental skills require extra review.
  [AI5] Deprecated skills are not integrated.
  [AI6] Integration must be traceable to DEC-XXX.
  [AI7] Integration must not break existing skills.
  [AI8] Integration must be tested before deployment.

## Auto-Integration Safety

Safety Checks:
  - Relevance score >= 80%
  - No duplicates
  - No conflicts with existing skills
  - Human approval obtained
  - DEC-XXX created
  - Tests pass

Rollback:
  - If integration fails, rollback to previous state
  - Restore from backup
  - Notify human
  - Document failure

## Auto-Integration Metrics

Track:
  - Skills discovered per project
  - Skills recommended per project
  - Skills integrated per project
  - Integration success rate
  - Time to integrate
  - Relevance score distribution

## Auto-Integration Commands

/sdd-discover-skills:
  Discover skills for current project
  Usage: /sdd-discover-skills --project=current

/sdd-recommend-skills:
  Recommend skills to add
  Usage: /sdd-recommend-skills --threshold=80

/sdd-integrate-skill:
  Integrate recommended skill
  Usage: /sdd-integrate-skill --skill=SKILL-XXX

/sdd-audit-skills:
  Audit current skill coverage
  Usage: /sdd-audit-skills

State: +
